---
import AboutHeroImage from "../assets/blog-placeholder-about.jpg";
import Layout from "../layouts/BlogPost.astro";
import BaseHead from "../components/BaseHead.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { SITE_TITLE } from "../consts";
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`About | ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description="Learn more about Juned Khan, Salesforce Developer and creator of Salesforce Dev Notes."
		/>
	</head>

	<body>
		<Header />

		<main class="container">
			<section class="hero">
				<h1>About Me</h1>

				<p class="subtitle">
					Salesforce Developer • Technical Writer • Lifelong Learner
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="content">
				<h2>Hello, I'm Juned 👋</h2>

				<p>
					I'm a Salesforce Developer passionate about building scalable
					applications, solving complex business problems, and sharing
					knowledge with the Salesforce community.
				</p>

				<p>
					Over the years, I've worked with Apex, Lightning Web Components,
					Integrations, APIs, Automation, and modern web technologies. This
					blog is where I document what I learn and share practical
					tutorials that help developers grow their Salesforce skills.
				</p>

				<h2>What You'll Find Here</h2>

				<div class="grid">
					<div class="card">
						<h3>Apex Development</h3>
						<p>
							Triggers, Classes, Batch Apex, Queueable Apex,
							SOQL, Governor Limits, and best practices.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="card">
						<h3>Lightning Web Components</h3>
						<p>
							Modern Salesforce UI development with practical
							examples and reusable components.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="card">
						<h3>Agentforce & AI</h3>
						<p>
							Exploring Salesforce AI capabilities and
							real-world Agentforce implementations.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="card">
						<h3>Integrations</h3>
						<p>
							REST APIs, Webhooks, Named Credentials,
							Authentication, and external systems.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<h2>My Mission</h2>

				<p>
					My goal is to create practical, easy-to-understand Salesforce
					content that helps developers learn faster and build better
					solutions.
				</p>

				<p>
					Instead of focusing only on theory, I prefer sharing real-world
					examples, implementation guides, troubleshooting techniques, and
					best practices that can be applied immediately.
				</p>

				<h2>Current Focus Areas</h2>

				<ul>
					<li>Salesforce Development</li>
					<li>Lightning Web Components (LWC)</li>
					<li>Agentforce & AI</li>
					<li>API Integrations</li>
					<!-- <li>System Design</li>
					<li>Full-Stack Development</li> -->
				</ul>

				<h2>Let's Connect</h2>

				<p>
					If you're a Salesforce developer, student, or technology
					enthusiast, I hope you find something useful here.
				</p>

				<p>
					Thanks for visiting and being part of this journey.
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>

		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.container {
		max-width: 1000px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 2rem;
	}

	.hero {
		text-align: center;
		padding: 4rem 0;
	}

	.hero h1 {
		font-size: 3rem;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
		color: #0176d3;
	}

	.subtitle {
		font-size: 1.2rem;
		color: #64748b;
	}

	.content h2 {
		margin-top: 3rem;
		color: #1e293b;
	}

	.content p {
		line-height: 1.8;
		color: #475569;
	}

	.grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
		gap: 1.5rem;
		margin-top: 2rem;
	}

	.card {
		padding: 1.5rem;
		border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
		border-radius: 12px;
		background: white;
	}

	.card h3 {
		color: #0176d3;
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}

	ul {
		padding-left: 1.5rem;
	}

	li {
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}
</style>
```
